# Rust build output
target/

# Ahead-of-time compiled plugin components (crates/wasm-host writes these
# beside each installed plugin; they are reproducible from the .wasm)
.aot/

# Reference source copies
3rds/

# Backup files
*.bak

# IDE / editor
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test output (generated, not committed)
tests/output/

# A recording the recorder made — the product feature, pointed anywhere. Never
# committed: it holds everything the model saw, in the clear.
tests/fixtures/cassettes/
recordings/

# Environment
.env
.env.local

# Per-session runtime artifacts under the project-local data dir
# (`local_data_dir = <cwd>/.agix/`). Project-*authored* content there —
# `.agix/agents/*.md`, `.agix/settings.json` — is meant to be committed, so
# this ignores the generated subdirectories rather than `.agix/` wholesale.
# `telemetry/` is new: sessions now record a JSONL transcript by default
# (previously nothing was recorded unless a caller passed an explicit path).
.agix/telemetry/
.agix/sessions/
.agix/teams/

# The per-machine settings overlay — same tier as `.agix/settings.json` but
# never committed. Written by the interactive permission prompt's
# "always allow, this project".
.agix/settings.local.json

# Intermediate-process documents (status assessments, comparison analyses,
# audit reports) — see CLAUDE.md §2. They describe what the system *was like*
# at a moment, not how it is built, and go stale the day they land. Conclusions
# belong in code, commit messages, or docs/ design notes.
.local/
